ding the total cost of fatal opioid overdose ($549,691 million) by the number of fatal opioid overdose cases (47,600)\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"These components were calculated by multiplying the number of state cases\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The 38 states and DC were ranked by per capita combined costs.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Cases of opioid use disorder were identified by using questions on opioid abuse or dependence during the past year.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"this study did not directly calculate state costs per case\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}